{
  "id": "a2-exponentials-04",
  "version": 2,
  "title": "Properties of logarithms",
  "xp": 18,
  "tags": [
    "algebra",
    "logarithms"
  ],
  "learn": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Logs turn multiplying into adding",
      "body": "Because logs are exponents, exponent rules become log rules. Product: $\\log_b(MN)=\\log_b M+\\log_b N$. Quotient: $\\log_b\\frac{M}{N}=\\log_b M-\\log_b N$. Power: $\\log_b(M^p)=p\\log_b M$."
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "Combine into one log",
      "body": "Use the rules in either direction.",
      "steps": [
        "$\\log_2 40-\\log_2 5=\\log_2\\frac{40}{5}$",
        "$=\\log_2 8=3$",
        "Likewise $\\log 2+\\log 50=\\log 100=2$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Change of base",
      "body": "A calculator may only have $\\log$ and $\\ln$. To reach any base, use $\\log_b x=\\frac{\\log x}{\\log b}$. So $\\log_2 5=\\frac{\\log 5}{\\log 2}\\approx 2.32$. Also beware: $\\log(a+b)$ is not $\\log a+\\log b$. There is no rule for a sum inside a log."
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "tip",
      "body": "Power rule example: $\\log_2 8^2=2\\log_2 8=2\\cdot 3=6$, and indeed $2^6=64=8^2$."
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "$\\log 2+\\log 50=$ ? (base 10)",
      "accepted": [
        "2"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$\\log(2\\cdot 50)=\\log 100=2$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "$\\log_2 40-\\log_2 5=$ ?",
      "accepted": [
        "3"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$\\log_2\\frac{40}{5}=\\log_2 8=3$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "Use the power rule: $\\log_2(8^2)=$ ?",
      "accepted": [
        "6"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$2\\log_2 8=2\\cdot 3=6$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "Condense $2\\log_3 x+\\log_3 5$.",
      "choices": [
        "$\\log_3(5x^2)$",
        "$\\log_3(10x)$",
        "$\\log_3(5x)^2$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "Power rule: $2\\log_3 x=\\log_3 x^2$. Product rule then gives $\\log_3(5x^2)$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "Which statement is false?",
      "choices": [
        "$\\log(ab)=\\log a+\\log b$",
        "$\\log\\frac{a}{b}=\\log a-\\log b$",
        "$\\log(a+b)=\\log a+\\log b$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "There is no rule that splits a sum. Try $a=b=10$: $\\log 20\\ne 2$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "Expand $\\log_b(x^3y)$.",
      "choices": [
        "$3\\log_b(x+y)$",
        "$3\\log_b x+\\log_b y$",
        "$\\log_b x^3\\cdot\\log_b y$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "Product rule splits it into $\\log_b x^3+\\log_b y$, then the power rule brings down 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "Using change of base, $\\log_2 5\\approx$ ? (2 decimals)",
      "accepted": [
        "2.32"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$\\frac{\\log 5}{\\log 2}\\approx\\frac{0.699}{0.301}\\approx 2.32$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "prompt": "$\\log_b\\frac{M}{N}=\\log_b M\\ \\_\\_\\ \\log_b N$",
      "choices": [
        "$+$",
        "$\\cdot$",
        "$-$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "Dividing inside the log subtracts the logs."
    }
  ]
}